🔎 Research Standards — Kurt Celvin

1. Purpose

Establish consistent standards for transparent, responsible, and reproducible public research.

2. Evidence

Distinguish documented facts, calculated results, interpretations, proposals, and unresolved questions. Cite sources for factual claims.

3. Methodology

Document methods, assumptions, inputs, dependencies, limitations, and uncertainty where applicable.

4. AI Use & Human Review

Disclose material AI assistance. Human review remains responsible for evaluating accuracy, context, and publication readiness.

5. Validation & Reproducibility

Test code where practical. Provide reproducible steps and explain results, errors, and known limitations.

6. Corrections & Versioning

Record material corrections, maintain meaningful version history, and identify superseded findings.

7. Privacy & Security

Never publish credentials, confidential records, private financial data, or unauthorized personal information.

8. Publication Integrity

Do not present hypotheses as proven facts or imply certification, endorsement, quantum advantage, or investment performance without adequate evidence.

9. Reuse & Attribution

Respect copyright, trademarks, third-party licenses, and attribution requirements. Specify reuse terms for original work when appropriate.

10. Human Responsibility

Research publication remains subject to human judgment, accountability, and applicable law.

